          conceptEn: "After a DOM change the browser may recompute geometry (layout), repaint pixels, and composite layers. If a style change invalidated geometry, reading `offsetHeight` can force synchronous layout. Repeatedly alternating such writes and reads in a loop is layout thrashing; batch reads before writes and inspect the profile. `transform` and `opacity` often avoid layout, but compositing is not guaranteed and extra layers cost memory. Measure the outcome on target devices.",
